# Dependencies & build output
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Playwright's browser-lane output (apps/web/e2e, once that app lands), both
# regenerated by the next run. `test-results/` is the per-test artifacts —
# traces and screenshots, which the config captures on failing tests only, so a
# green run leaves nothing there but Playwright's own `.last-run.json`;
# `playwright-report/` is the HTML report, which the reporter writes on every
# run, green ones included.
# Unanchored so they match wherever a config puts them.
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Agent git worktrees (created by .claude tooling inside the repo)
.claude/worktrees/

# Environment & secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
*.log

# Course content — the repo never contains real lecture material
# (CLAUDE.md Hard constraints). Course files live in the data directory
# `resolveDataDir` (apps/server/src/data-directory.ts) names; `data/` is the
# conventional name for one set inside a checkout. This block is the floor that
# keeps them out of `git add`; the rule is
# .claude/scripts/check-no-course-content.sh, whose harness fails if a ban here is
# one the gate does not flag. The synthetic eval deck is authored as text under
# eval/, never as one of these. The `!` lines re-include the gate's one exemption,
# synthetic ingest fixtures (owner decision 2026-10-19, #31); the harness fails if
# the gate does not exempt them.
data/
*.pdf
*.pptx
*.ppt
*.key
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
!/packages/ingest/fixtures/*.pdf
!/packages/ingest/fixtures/*.pptx
